# 0001. One repo, symlinked into ~, split into numbered conf.d files

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

The shell config lives in this git repo, is linked into `~` by a script, and is split into
one-job files loaded in name order.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: the old single `~/.zshrc` grew by hand on two machines (a Mac and an Arch
  desktop), appended PATH lines to itself (3,249 PATH entries, 21 unique) and held
  credentials. Changes on one machine never reached the other.
- **Entry point**: `~/.zshrc` is a symlink to `zshrc`. It sources p10k's instant prompt first,
  finds the repo through the symlink (`ZSH_CONFIG_DIR=${${(%):-%x}:A:h}`), then sources
  `conf.d/*.zsh(N)` in name order and nothing else.
- **conf.d, one job per file**:
  - `00-env.zsh`: XDG dirs, `ZSH_CACHE_DIR`, `EDITOR`, `IS_MAC`/`IS_LINUX`, PATH and fzf look;
    spawns no processes.
  - `10-options.zsh`: setopt, history, key bindings.
  - `20-plugins.zsh`: zinit and plugins ([0002](0002-zinit-turbo-plugins.adr)).
  - `30-completion.zsh`: compinit, zstyles, fzf-tab.
  - `40-tools.zsh`: cached tool inits and completions ([0003](0003-startup-budget-cached-inits.adr)).
  - `50-aliases.zsh`, `60-functions.zsh`, `70-devops.zsh` (docker, k8s, terraform, aws).
  - `90-local.zsh`: untracked machine settings and secrets, last ([0006](0006-secrets-out-of-repo-gitleaks.adr)).
  - `lib/git.zsh`: git helpers, loaded after oh-my-zsh's git plugin.
- **Linking**: `scripts/link.sh link|unlink|status` (`make link`, `make unlink`,
  `make status`) links `zshrc`, `git/config`, `git/ignore`, `git/hooks`, `direnv/direnvrc`,
  `atuin/config.toml`, `lazygit/config.yml` and `eza/theme.yml` into `~` / `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.
  An existing file is moved to `<file>.bak-<YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS>`; replacing an old `~/.zshrc` also
  runs `migrate-secrets.sh` on the backup. `unlink` restores the newest backup. A new file to
  link is one line in the `links=(...)` array.
- **Install**: `make install` = `make deps` (`scripts/install-deps.sh`, brew or pacman) +
  `make link`; `make chsh` makes zsh the login shell on Arch.
- **Consequences**: `git pull` + `reload` syncs both machines; history and review come with
  git. Load order is the file-name order, so the numbering is part of the contract. Editing
  `~/.zshrc` edits the repo; `.bak-*` files are not the config.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: zsh, bash (`link.sh`), GNU Make, git.
- Alternatives: one big `.zshrc`: hard to navigate, conflicts between machines; a dotfiles
  manager (chezmoi, stow, yadm): another tool for what a 60-line script does.
